-- title:
--   Compute and retain the two local reporting counts
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural half-size $h$ and set $L=512h$, $C=\binom Lh$, and $P=\binom L{2h}\binom{2h}h$. Let a two-cell destination $z$ end by scratch base $f$. Assume $f+(L+1)^2$ fits in space, space fits in a word, $512$, $2^{L+1}$, and $P$ fit in a word, and $d+L+3$ fits in the depth limit. The fixed program returns and stores
--   $$
--   r=P,\qquad \mu'(z)=C,\qquad \mu'(z+1)=P.
--   $$
--   It takes $\operatorname{buildTime}(L)+300$ steps and preserves memory below $z$.
--
--   These are the local subset and ordered disjoint-pair counts retained in the shared reporting header.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightSharedReportingCounts.lean#L27-L99

